  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "An empty cell as a first date is serial 0, but a logical in that cell is #VALUE!",
  "statement": "A reference to an empty cell as the first date of these functions reads as serial 0 and gives a normal answer: NETWORKDAYS(B1,5) is 4 and WORKDAY(B1,2) is 3. YEARFRAC(B1,5,0) is 5/360. TRUE in the same cell gives #VALUE!, as a direct TRUE does, so a blank is not treated as the logical FALSE either.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "8 recorded readings with an empty B1, one per function, each paired with a reading with TRUE in B1.",
